1 Introduction
**************

Harmless is a coding harness written in Emacs Lisp.  It is not gptel.
It does not wrap Grok Build, Claude Code, or the Codex CLI. It talks to
a model provider itself, keeps the transcript in Emacs, and runs tools
in the project directory.

   A session is one conversation.  It is pinned to one connection and
one model.  Several sessions can run in one Emacs.  One can use Grok,
another a local model, and a third Claude, each in its own project.

   The transcript buffer is a view.  The saved session on disk is the
record.  Closing the buffer does not delete the session.

   Harmless requires GNU Emacs 31.


