2 Installation
**************

Put the ‘lisp’ directory on ‘load-path’ and load the package.

     (add-to-list 'load-path "~/programming/emacs/harmless/lisp")
     (require 'harmless)

   Choose the connections Harmless may use.  Most people need one.

     (setq harmless-providers (list (harmless-make-xai))
           harmless-default-model "grok-4.6"
           harmless-default-reasoning-effort "xhigh")

   The constructors are ‘harmless-make-xai’, ‘harmless-make-openai’,
‘harmless-make-anthropic’, and ‘harmless-make-openai-compat’.  Each
takes an optional connection name.  The default names are ‘xAI’,
‘OpenAI’, and ‘Anthropic’.  A second account needs its own name, such as
‘xAI work’.

   Settings can live in your init file or in ‘config.el’ under
‘harmless-directory’.  That directory defaults to ‘harmless’ inside
‘user-emacs-directory’, so a typical path is
‘~/.emacs.d/harmless/config.el’.  Harmless loads ‘config.el’ once, the
first time a command needs it.

   If ‘harmless-providers’ is empty, ‘M-x harmless’ asks you to pick a
provider and a connection name.

   A local OpenAI-compatible server looks like this:

     (setq harmless-providers
           (list (harmless-make-openai-compat
                  "local"
                  :host "127.0.0.1:11434"
                  :protocol "http"
                  :endpoint "/v1/chat/completions"
                  :key "none"
                  :models '("llama3.2"))))


