5 Transcript
************

The transcript is read-only.  Replies are Markdown.  A tool call is a
folded line.  A run of reads and searches folds into one ‘explored’
line.

‘TAB’
     Toggle the fold at point.

‘S-TAB’
     Toggle every fold.

‘LEFT’
     Close the fold at point.

‘RIGHT’
     Open the fold at point.

‘RET’
     Move to the prompt.

‘i’
     Move to the prompt.

‘q’
     Quit the window.

‘k’
     Compact the transcript.

‘w’
     Rewind to the turn at point.

‘E’
     Edit the prompt at point and rerun from there.

‘f’
     Fork through the turn at point.

   ‘k’, or ‘M-x harmless-compact’, summarizes the older turns and
replaces them with one summary.  The recent turns stay in the
transcript.  A turn starts at a user message and includes the assistant
reply and tool results that follow it.  The default keeps the last two
turns (‘harmless-compact-keep-turns’).  A numeric prefix argument sets
how many turns to keep, and the command keeps at least one.  An empty
summary leaves the transcript as it was.  A turn that is streaming or
waiting on permission is left alone.  The same command is ‘k’ in the
Harmless menu.

   When the last prompt has used at least ‘harmless-compact-threshold’
percent of the model's context window, the next prompt compacts first.
The default is 80.  The same percent applies to every model.  A model
with a larger window compacts at the same fullness.  Nil turns automatic
compact off.  A model with no known window is left alone.  An automatic
compact that fails still sends the prompt.

   ‘w’, or ‘M-x harmless-rewind’, drops every turn after the one at
point and saves the shorter transcript.  That turn stays, including its
assistant reply and tool results.  A numeric prefix argument keeps that
many turns from the start of the transcript.  Outside the transcript,
the command asks which turn to keep.  It keeps at least one turn and
asks before dropping anything.  The dropped turns are not saved.  The
last prompt size is cleared, and the running token totals stay.  A turn
that is streaming or waiting on permission is left alone.  The same
command is ‘w’ in the Harmless menu.

   ‘E’, or ‘M-x harmless-edit-prompt’, replaces the prompt at point and
sends the new text.  The reply to the old prompt, and every turn after
it, is dropped and is not saved.  A numeric prefix argument chooses the
turn, counting from the start of the transcript.  Outside the
transcript, the command asks which turn to edit.  It asks before
changing anything.  The last prompt size is cleared, and the running
token totals stay.  A turn that is streaming or waiting on permission is
left alone.  The same command is ‘E’ in the Harmless menu.

   ‘f’, or ‘M-x harmless-fork’, copies the transcript through the turn
at point into a new session.  That turn stays in the copy, including its
assistant reply and tool results.  Later turns stay in the original
session.  The original session is left unchanged.  Nothing is sent.  A
numeric prefix argument chooses the turn, counting from the start of the
transcript.  Outside the transcript, the command asks which turn to copy
through.  It asks before creating the new session.  The copy starts with
empty token totals.  A turn that is streaming or waiting on permission
is left alone.  The same command is ‘f’ in the Harmless menu.

   Click the model name in the header line to change the connection, the
model, and the effort.  *Note Models::.


