10 Tools
********

The model does not change your files by printing a diff.  It calls
tools.  You see each call in the transcript.  Permission rules are in
*note Permissions::.

   Tool calls in one reply run together.  Harmless asks for permission
one call at a time.  An allowed call starts before the next question, so
several shell commands overlap.  Results are added to the transcript in
the order the model requested them.  Abort cancels the calls that are
still running.

   Paths are relative to the project root unless you pass an absolute
path that is still inside that root.  A path that escapes the project is
refused.  An empty path is refused.  The filesystem root is not a
project: a search there is refused, and Harmless will not store its own
state there.

   A detached chat is offered ‘memory_read’, ‘memory_remember’,
‘memory_write_topic’, and ‘ask_user’.  *Note Memory::.  *Note
Questions::.  It can list live sessions and send one a finding.  *Note
Messages::.  It can search the web and fetch a page.  *Note Web
search::.  *Note Fetch a page::.  It can search X for posts, a thread,
and accounts.  *Note X search::.  It can list and read MCP resources.
*Note MCP::.  It can see the screen, click, type, and open a browser.
*Note Computer use::.

* Menu:

* File tools::  Read, list, write, replace, and patch.
* Search::      Find files and lines.
* Shell::       Run a command.
* Questions::   Ask one question with choices.
* Subagents::   A child session that reports a summary.
* Workflows::   One script, many child sessions, one result.
* Worktrees::   Isolated checkouts of the same repository.
* Messages::    A finding sent to another live session.
* Web search::  Look up a query on the web.
* Fetch a page::  Read one http or https page.
* X search::    Find posts, a thread, and accounts on X.
* MCP::         Call a configured server and read its resources.
* Computer use::  See the screen, click, type, and open a browser.
* Monitors::    Wake when a line in a file or a stream matches.


