18 Trouble
**********

‘M-x harmless-abort’, or ‘a’ in the transcript, or ‘C-c C-a’ in the
prompt, cancels the HTTP request or a foreground shell command.  A
background shell keeps running.  A subagent that is still running is
aborted too, and its summary is not added to the transcript.  A workflow
that is still running is aborted the same way, and its one result is not
added.  A checkout that session entered stays on disk.  The session
returns to idle and the transcript records ‘aborted’.

   An empty reply from the model is an error: ‘The model returned an
empty reply.’

   Diagnostic lines go to the buffer ‘*harmless-log*’.  The buffer keeps
at most ‘harmless-log-max-lines’ lines (2000).  Do not put an API key in
a note you expect to see there.  The log is not written to disk.

   ‘M-x harmless-reload-all-harmless’ loads every ‘.el’ file beside the
‘harmless.el’ Emacs actually loaded.  It skips ‘harmless-autoloads.el’
and prefers a newer source file over a byte-compiled copy.  Restart
Emacs when a live session was created before a session field was added.
Reloading does not rebuild this manual.  *Note Manual::.


